{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The sensitive seams match the reviewed design: both nil bytes and the not-found sentinel still produce “missing,” while invalid addresses and mismatched bytes return nil. Admission retains the covered-name check and local refusal construction, and the call-runtime change still uses linear sequencing with tail marking. PHP’s `site-set-of` gains the explicitly authorized `:tree` return key; it does not enter the serialized record.\n"}}
