{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '245,267p' collab/exception-track/1795020669393-architect-yang-dedup-round2-audit.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md\nsed -n '1,65p' src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc\nsed -n '1,26p' src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\nsed -n '43,115p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc\nsed -n '100,142p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"       [nodes]\n       (reduce (fn [acc node] (app* 'php/vconj acc node)) (u/lit []) nodes))\n     ```\n   - Round 1 wired Python (`lower.cljc:236`) and TypeScript (`lower.cljc:181`) to [core/lower.cljc:109-111](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/lower.cljc#L109-L111) (`(core/build-vector 'php/vconj nodes)`), missing PHP's `args-vector` because of its different name. (Also [php/antlr/lower.cljc:274-276](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc#L274-L276) wraps `core/app*` in `(defn- app* [op-sym & args] (apply core/app* op-sym args))` instead of `(def ^:private app* core/app*)` as in Python and TypeScript.)\n3. **Inlined `core/definitions->uast` in `python/antlr/prelude.cljc` and `yang.core.call`:**\n   - [python/antlr/prelude.cljc:3684-3686](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc#L3684-L3686):\n     ```clojure\n     (defn- definitions->uast\n       [defs]\n       (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n     ```\n     which is verbatim [core/prelude.cljc:196-198](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc#L196-L198) (`(core/definitions->uast defs)`).\n   - [core/call.cljc:158-165](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc#L158-L165):\n     ```clojure\n     (def uast\n       \"The bundled definitions, in source order and tail marked.\"\n       (u/mark-tails\n         (reduce (fn [ast [key form]]\n                   (u/then ast (u/def! key (u/sexp->uast form))))\n                 (u/def! (ffirst definitions)\n                         (u/sexp->uast (second (first definitions))))\n                 (rest definitions))))\n     ```\n(ns yang.core.prelude\n  \"Emitter machinery shared by every language's runtime-profile prelude\n   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md §17, lift L1). A language supplies its\n   module's own namespace string, its uninit sentinel, its definition list\n   and its refusal namespace; everything here is a pure function of those.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(defn define\n  \"`(yin/def (quote key) form)` in prelude notation: the key quoted, so\n   `sexp->uast` reads it as the literal symbol Rule R requires.\"\n  [key form]\n  (list 'yin/def (list 'quote key) form))\n\n\n(defn strip\n  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `ns-str`; any other value as it\n   is. Qualified internal store keys stay qualified.\"\n  [ns-str sym]\n  (if (and (symbol? sym) (= ns-str (namespace sym)))\n    (symbol (name sym))\n    sym))\n\n\n(defn strip-form\n  \"A prelude-notation form with every symbol `strip`ped: references,\n   definition keys and quoted keys alike. Keywords, strings and the\n   keys of literal maps are untouched.\"\n  [ns-str form]\n  (walk/postwalk (partial strip ns-str) form))\n\n\n(defn placeholder\n  \"The `[k uninit]` definition for runtime key `k`, so each read of it is\n   discharged by an unconditional module-level definition.\"\n  [k uninit]\n  [k uninit])\n\n\n(defn module-definitions\n  \"The module's definition list: a `uninit` placeholder for every runtime\n   key (stripped of `ns-str`), then every definition, stripped.\"\n  [ns-str uninit runtime-keys definitions]\n  (into (mapv (fn [k] (placeholder (strip ns-str k) uninit)) runtime-keys)\n        (map (fn [[k form]] [(strip ns-str k) (strip-form ns-str form)]))\n        definitions))\n\n\n(defn wide-app\n  \"One application whose operands are `nodes` (in order), applied to a lambda\n   with one parameter per node that returns nil. Every operand runs on the main sequence before the one call, so the\n   linker's scanners discharge every body read of a sibling or runtime key;\n   a `then` chain would nest definitions in closure bodies.\"\n  [nodes]\n  (let [params (mapv (fn [i] (symbol (str \"%d\" i))) (range (count nodes)))]\n    (u/mark-tails (apply u/app (u/lam params (u/lit nil)) nodes))))\n\n\n(defn module-tree\n  \"The module tree for `defs` (`[key form]`, already stripped) followed by\n   the `trailing` UAST nodes.\"\n(ns yang.core.call\n  \"Language-neutral guest calling convention (docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n   §8.10). This namespace emits the same pure definitions into bundled\n   preludes and the linked `yang.call` module.\"\n  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module that publishes the shared calling runtime.\"\n  'yang.call)\n\n\n(def host-names\n  \"Host module names read by the guest definitions.\"\n  '#{cell/get cell/authentic? data/callable? data/contains? data/count\n     data/map? data/nth data/string? data/vector?})\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The one ordered definition list used by both emitters.\"\n  '[;; Descriptor projection remains structural after callable admission,\n    ;; with one ruling-of-record refinement: a `:cell-ref`-shaped map is\n    ;; dereferenced only when the heap authenticates it (`cell/authentic?`,\n    ;; the issuer's own answer). A map that imitates the reference language\n    ;; is data, so it projects to itself and its fate follows the ordinary\n        set-address (jing/materialize! handle (vec set))\n        record {:yang.site/manifest manifest, :yang.site/root root,\n                :yang.site/revision frontend-revision,\n                :yang.site/profile profile-address, :yang.site/set set-address}]\n    {:record record, :record-address (jing/materialize! handle record),\n     :set-address set-address, :set set}))\n\n\n(defn- read-at\n  [handle address]\n  (when (jing/segment-address? address)\n    (let [bytes ((:get-bytes-fn handle) address ::absent)]\n      (cond\n        (or (nil? bytes) (= ::absent bytes)) ::absent\n        (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bytes) (jing/segment-value address bytes)))))\n\n\n(defn verify\n  \"Read and verify a published set, or return nil for missing or mismatched\n   metadata. An empty set is a valid publication.\"\n  [handle manifest record-address]\n  (let [module (read-at handle manifest)\n        record (read-at handle record-address)\n        sites (read-at handle (when (map? record) (:yang.site/set record)))]\n    (when (and (map? module) (map? record) (vector? sites)\n               (= manifest (:yang.site/manifest record))\n               (= (:yin.module/tree module) (:yang.site/root record))\n               (= frontend-revision (:yang.site/revision record))\n               (= profile-address (:yang.site/profile record))\n               (every? (fn [entry]\n                         (and (vector? entry) (= 2 (count entry))\n                              (vector? (first entry))\n                              (let [mark (second entry)\n                                    kind (if (vector? mark) (first mark) mark)]\n                                (contains? #{:call :line :loop} kind))))\n                       sites)\n               (= sites (safepoint/site-set (into {} sites))))\n      {:record record, :set sites})))\n\n\n(defn signed-entry\n  \"Sign the association between a published manifest and its site record.\"\n  [key manifest record-address]\n  (publication/signed-entry key manifest record-address))\n\n\n(defn entry-datoms\n  \"Index signed site publications alongside name assertions.\"\n  [signed]\n  (publication/entry-datoms signed))\n\n\n(defn discover\n  \"Find site record addresses signed by a declared public key for manifest.\"\n  [datoms publics manifest]\n  (let [proofs (reduce (fn [acc [e a v]]\n                         (cond-> acc\n                           (= a :yang.site/proof) (update e (fnil conj #{}) v)))\n                       {} datoms)]\n    (vec (distinct\n           (keep (fn [[e a env]]\n                   (when (and (= a :yang.site/envelope) (map? env)\n                              (= :publish (:yang.site/op env))\n                              (= manifest (:yang.site/manifest env)))\n                     (let [ps (get proofs e)\n                           sig (when (= 1 (count ps))\n                                 (:yin.module/signature (first ps)))]\n                       (when (and (string? sig)\n                                  (some #(and (= (:yin.module/asserted-by env)\n                                                 (sign/principal %))\n                                              (sign/verify-envelope\n                                                % (jing/canonical-bytes env) sig))\n                                        publics))\n    {:record r,\n     :record-address (jing/materialize! handle r),\n     :set-address set-address,\n     :set set}))\n\n\n(defn- read-at\n  \"The value at `address` in `handle`: `::absent` when the handle holds no\n   bytes for a segment address (the handle is asked with a not-found\n   sentinel, as a byte store is), nil when `address` is no segment address\n   or its bytes do not hash to it, else the value.\"\n  [handle address]\n  (if-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n    nil\n    (let [bs ((:get-bytes-fn handle) address ::absent)]\n      (cond\n        (= ::absent bs) ::absent\n        (nil? bs) ::absent\n        (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs) (jing/segment-value address bs)\n        :else nil))))\n\n\n(defn- absent?\n  [x]\n  (= ::absent x))\n\n\n(defn- missing\n  \"The stage's report of the absent `address`: first one met, nothing\n   written.\"\n  [address]\n  {:status :missing, :address address})\n\n\n(defn- fetch\n  \"The value at `address` in `handle`, or nil when absent or not its\n   address.\"\n  [handle address]\n  (let [v (read-at handle address)]\n    (when-not (absent? v) v)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
